  "term": "hypericin",
  "definition": "Hypericin is a naturally occurring compound found in St. John’s wort, a plant associated with antidepressant effects. It appears to affect the brain’s handling of several chemical messengers, including serotonin, norepinephrine, and dopamine, which may help explain its mood-related effects.",
